# Usage: This task must be executed when the user says: "register a component in SitecoreAI". It must use the marketer MCP server.

## Variable resolution (do this first, do not skip)

Replace variables using these rules:

- `{{TemplateName}} = "{{ComponentName}}"`
- `{{ComponentName}} = "{{ComponentName}}"`
- `{{TSXComponentName}} = "{{ComponentName}}"`
- `{{TemplateFolderName}} = "{{ComponentName}}"`
- `{{RenderingFolderName}} = "{{ComponentName}} Renderings"`
- `{{AvailableRenderingsItem}} = "/sitecore/content/johnson-matthey/matthey-corporate-website/Presentation/Available Renderings/Johnson Matthey"`
- `{{DataFolderName}} = pluralize({{ComponentName}})`
- `{{ComponentTemplatesPath}} = "/sitecore/templates/Project/johnson-matthey"`
- `{{PlaceholdersPath}} = "/sitecore/layout/Placeholder Settings/Project/johnson-matthey"`
- `{{RootWebsitePath}} = "/sitecore/content/johnson-matthey/matthey-corporate-website"`
- `{{HomeWebsitePath}} = "/sitecore/content/johnson-matthey/matthey-corporate-website/home"`
- `{{ComponentsFolder}} = "/sitecore/layout/Renderings/Project/johnson-matthey"`
- `{{MediaFolder}} = "/sitecore/media library/Project/johnson-matthey/matthey-corporate-website"`
- `{{DataTemplateIcon}} = ""`
- `{{FolderTemplateIcon}} = "/sitecore/shell/themes/standard/Applications/32x32/folder.png"`

System templates:

- `{{StandardTemplate}} = "/sitecore/templates/System/Templates/Standard template"`
- `{{TemplateSectionTemplate}} = "/sitecore/templates/System/Templates/Template section"`
- `{{TemplateFieldTemplate}} = "/sitecore/templates/System/Templates/Template field"`
- `{{PlaceholderTemplate}} = "/sitecore/templates/System/Layout/Placeholder"`
- `{{PerSiteStandardValues}} = "/sitecore/templates/Foundation/Experience Accelerator/StandardValues/_PerSiteStandardValues"`
- `{{FolderBaseTemplate}} = "/sitecore/templates/Common/Folder"`
- `{{BaseRenderingParametersTemplate}} = "/sitecore/templates/Foundation/JSS Experience Accelerator/Presentation/Rendering Parameters/BaseRenderingParameters"`
- `{{IDynamicPlaceholder}} = "/sitecore/templates/Foundation/Experience Accelerator/Dynamic Placeholders/Rendering Parameters/IDynamicPlaceholder"`
- `{{IRenderingId}} = "/sitecore/templates/Foundation/Experience Accelerator/Markup Decorator/Rendering Parameters/IRenderingId"`
- `{{RenderingFolderTemplate}} = "/sitecore/templates/Foundation/JSS Experience Accelerator/Multisite/Folders/Rendering Folder"`
- `{{RenderingTemplate}} = "/sitecore/templates/Foundation/JavaScript Services/Json Rendering"`

## Template field source rules (apply when creating fields)

- Image fields: set **Source** = `query:$siteMedia`
- Rich Text fields: set **Source** = `query:$xaRichTextProfile`
- General Link fields: set **Source** = `query:$linkableHomes`
- For General Link + Image fields: set **Shared** = `true`

## IMPORTANT execution rules (hard constraints)

1. **Standard values rules**
   - For any **LinkField** in any `__Standard Values` item: set its standard value to point to `{{HomeWebsitePath}}` (ID-based value).
   - For any **DropLink** field in any `__Standard Values` item: set its standard value to point to `{{HomeWebsitePath}}` (ID-based value).
   - For any **General Link** field in any `__Standard Values` item: don't set a default value.

2. **Verification & traceability**
   - After creating any item/template, immediately retrieve it and verify it exists.
   - Always return the created item’s **ID and full path**.
   - Persist and reuse these references in later steps:
     - `{{GeneratedComponentTemplatesRoot}}`
     - `{{GeneratedDataTemplate}}`
     - `{{GeneratedDataTemplateDataSection}}`
     - `{{GeneratedDataTemplateStandardValuesItem}}`
     - `{{GeneratedDataFolderTemplate}}`
     - `{{GeneratedDataFolderTemplateStandardValuesItem}}`
     - `{{GeneratedRenderingTemplate}}`
     - `{{GeneratedDataFolderItem}}`
     - `{{GeneratedDataItem}}`
     - `{{GeneratedRenderingFolderItem}}`
     - `{{GeneratedRenderingItem}}`
     - `{{PlaceholderItem}}` (only if created)

## Automation (Marketer MCP) — for future prompts

- **Use the marketer MCP** server identifier: `user-marketer` (not `user-marketer2`).
- **For every "register a component" / "register components in Sitecore" request:** follow this rule from the top: resolve variables first, then execute Steps 1–8 in order. Return a structured result with ID + full path for each created/updated item and all stored variables.
- **All steps are normal item operations.** The rule describes creating and updating items (parent + template + name + fields). There is no separate "template API": a Template Section is created by adding a child item with the Template Section template; a Template Field by adding a child under the Data section with the Template Field template; `__Standard Values` by adding a child under the data template with the data template as its template; and so on. Use marketer MCP tools accordingly: **create_child_item** / **create_content_item** for new items (with the correct `parentId`, `templateId`, `name`, `path`, and `fields` where applicable), **update_fields_on_content_item** / **update_content** to set Type, Source, Shared, `__Standard values`, `__Masters`, and other field values, **get_content_item_by_path** / **get_content_item_by_id** to resolve IDs and verify after each step. Execute every step as written; do not skip steps on the assumption that template tree is unsupported. If a specific call fails, report the error and which steps remain.

